format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

lesson half-life
title: Half-life
minutes: 6
xp: 60
teaches: u2-half-life-meaning
teaches: u2-half-life-pattern
teaches: u2-half-life-group
relies_on: u2-random-single

description:
    How fast does a group of radioactive nuclei fade? You will look at 100 unstable nuclei, find the pattern, and see why half-life is about a crowd and not a timer inside each atom.

cite ref-epa-radioactive-decay
supports: Half-life is the time for half of the radioactive atoms to decay; it ranges from seconds to billions of years.

cite ref-openstax-up3-10-3
supports: Half-life and the exponential decay curve.

cite ref-openstax-chem-21-3
supports: Each radioactive nuclide has a characteristic, constant half-life.

card c01
kind: item
