item: u2-l3-fill-pattern

card c06
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: The numbers are a pattern
figure: half-life-bars
figure_at: 1

body:
    Start with 100. After one half-life, about 50 are left. After two, about 25. Then about 12, then about 6. It says about every time, because each count is a pattern and not an exact number.

card c16
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l3-match-halves

card c07
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l3-tom-gone

card c08
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: A group, not a timer
figure: group-not-timer
figure_at: 1

body:
    Remember the first lesson: you cannot say when one nucleus will change. A big group is different, because it follows a pattern. Half-life describes the whole group. It is not a timer inside each atom.

